{"id":"resp_80974ff851bd645e","created_at":1795617987,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_b805b506a9715b14","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We're asked to \"Revise previous_candidate: the COMPLETE latest SHACL, bound to candidate_version and candidate_sha256. Return the COMPLETE revised SHACL in one <BEGIN_SHACL> ... <END_SHACL> block. No regeneration or partial patch.\"\n\nWe need to make corrections per findings.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. ADMISSION_SCOPE_ERROR: target classes beyond declared population. Need to constrain activation to supplied population boundary. Likely need to add sh:targetNode? Actually we have a targetClass nltl:ship which is the declared owner_class. The admission error says \"Other target classes select beyond declared population\" and expects to use declared owner_class under mandatory evaluation-only complete-population guard; do not request fixture identities or invent eligibility selectors. Suggest \"Constrain activation to the supplied population boundary.\" So maybe need to add sh:targetClass with sh:scope? Might need to add sh:targetNode? But likely we need to add a sh:property with sh:path sh:targetClass? Actually we can add sh:node and sh:property? Not sure. Probably use sh:targetClass as is is fine, but need to add sh:nodeKind? But the system expects we add sh:sourceConstraint? Possibly we need to add sh:node on ship shape with sh:targetClass already. Might need to add sh:property sh:class nltl:ship? But it's already targetClass.\n\nBetter: Use sh:targetClass only, no other targetClass elsewhere. There is only ship shape targetClass. So maybe need to add sh:targetClass to limit activation with sh:node? Actually could add sh:targetClass with sh:condition? However the suggestion says \"Constrain activation to the supplied population boundary.\" Possibly add sh:node with sh:targetClass and sh:property sh:in? Hmm.\n\nWe may add a sh:property with sh:path a (rdf:type) and sh:hasValue nltl:ship? That would restrict to nodes that are of class ship only.\n\nAdd to _:ShipShape a property that ensures rdf:type = nltl:ship.\n\nAdd:\n\nsh:property [\n  sh:path rdf:type ;\n  sh:hasValue nltl:ship ;\n  sh:description \"Activation confined to declared ship population\" ;\n].\n\n2. CANONICAL_IDENTIFIER_ERROR for numericValue: need replace identifier with http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue (currently uses http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path? Actually the path uses sh:numericValue? Let's check the previous SHACL lines:\n\nIn QuantityShape:\n\nsh:path qudt:numericValue ; (currently uses qudt:numericValue?). Wait earlier they used qudt:numericValue? Yes earlier they wrote:\n\nsh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n\nBut finding says identifier used is http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#numericValue (that's wrong). So need to change path to http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue. So replace prefix? Use full IRI.\n\nThus modify sh:path to <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue>.\n\nAlso for unit: replace with <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit>.\n\n3. CANONICAL_IDENTIFIER_ERROR for class: sh:class for quantity was http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#QuantityValue, need http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue.\n\nSo change sh:class in asBuiltPlateThickness property: currently sh:class qudt:QuantityValue; need full IRI? Actually should be <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>.\n\n4. PATH_CONTRACT_ERROR: Complete property path conflicts with explicit ownership contract. It indicates path for polarClass should be ship->polarClass but also maybe the shape has a target shape? The path conflict maybe due to sh:targetClass for ship shape and shipShape includes property polarClass? Actually the ship shape only ensures hasSteelGradeRequirementCase. No polarClass path there. The conflict might be that the path for polarClass is defined on ship, but model expects path from ship to polarClass through hasSteelGradeRequirementCase? Hard to interpret. The suggestion: \"Follow the evidenced complete path; preserve the remaining obligation.\"\n\nThe evidence shows modelPaths includes path from ship to polarClassValue via polarClass directly (owner ship). So we should keep polarClass property maybe defined on ship directly. That's already correct: there is a property in SteelGradeRequirementCaseShape for polarClass, but maybe should be in ShipShape? Actually requirement: polarClass is a property of ship (as indicated in source). The shape currently defines polarClass under SteelGradeRequirementCaseShape (owner steelGradeRequirementCase). That's likely wrong; should be on ship.\n\nThus we need to move polarClass property to ShipShape, not SteelGradeRequirementCaseShape.\n\nSo modify: In ShipShape, add a property for polarClass (sh:path nltl:polarClass, sh:class nltl:polarClassValue, sh:minCount 1). And remove polarClass property from SteelGradeRequirementCaseShape.\n\nAlso need to adjust modelPaths owners maybe.\n\n5. UNRESOLVED_CONTEXT warning not blocking; but we will keep consistent with changes.\n\nThus revised SHACL:\n\n- Keep prefixes.\n\n- ShipShape: targetClass nltl:ship; add property for polarClass; optionally property to enforce rdf:type.\n\n- Add activation constraint via rdf:type hasValue.\n\n- Keep hasSteelGradeRequirementCase property.\n\n- SteelGradeRequirementCaseShape: remove polarClass property; keep other properties.\n\n- Update asBuiltPlateThickness property class to full IRI.\n\n- Update QuantityShape: fix numericValue and unit identifiers.\n\n- Update QuantityShape property for unit i.e., sh:in currently contains IRI <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM> which maybe fine.\n\nAlso need to adjust sh:nodeKind maybe not needed.\n\nLet's construct final SHACL text.\n\nNote: must use full IRIs for replaced identifiers.\n\nUse <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue> and <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit> and class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>.\n\nAlso for asBuiltPlateThickness property: sh:class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue>.\n\nAdd activation property:\n\nIn ShipShape add property:\n\nsh:path rdf:type;\nsh:hasValue nltl:ship;\n\nMake sure prefixes include rdf.\n\nWe need not remove others.\n\nNow produce full SHACL block.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_b0fac60a7c41a6a1","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Ship shape – every ship must be linked to a steel‑grade requirement case\n# and must have a polar class value. Activation is confined to the declared\n# ship population.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:ShipShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    # Activation guard – only nodes typed as nltl:ship are evaluated\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path rdf:type ;\n        sh:hasValue nltl:ship ;\n        sh:description \"Activation confined to the declared ship population\" ;\n    ] ;\n    # Ship must have a polar class value\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:polarClass ;\n        sh:class nltl:polarClassValue ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Polar class of the ship (I2.12.1).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    # Ship must be linked to at least one steel‑grade requirement case\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:hasSteelGradeRequirementCase ;\n        sh:class nltl:steelGradeRequirementCase ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Each ship must have an associated steel‑grade requirement case for its hull plating (I2.12.1).\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Steel‑grade requirement case shape – captures the inputs that drive the\n# lookup in Table 8 and the required hull‑structural steel grade.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:SteelGradeRequirementCaseShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:steelGradeRequirementCase ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:steelGradeRequirementCasePlating ;\n        sh:class nltl:plating ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Plating component to which this steel‑grade requirement applies (I2.12.1).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:asBuiltPlateThickness ;\n        sh:class <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue> ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:node _:QuantityShape ;\n        sh:description \"As‑built plate thickness (quantity) required for the lookup.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:steelMaterialClass ;\n        sh:class nltl:steelMaterialClassValue ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Material class of the structural members (I2.12.1).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:requiredHullStructuralSteelGrade ;\n        sh:class nltl:steelGradeValue ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Required hull‑structural steel grade.  The grade must be **not less than** the grade given in Table 8 for the combination of thickness, polar class and material class (I2.12.1).\" ;\n        sh:message \"Lookup against Table 8 (I2.12.1) is required; table data not provided in the current evidence set – constraint is recorded as unresolved.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:tableReference ;\n        sh:class nltl:tableReferenceValue ;\n        sh:hasValue nltl:iacsUrI2Table8 ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Explicit reference to IACS UR I2 Table 8 that supplies the allowable steel grades.\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Quantity shape – used for As‑built plate thickness\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n_:QuantityShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue> ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:description \"Numeric value of the quantity (e.g., plate thickness).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit> ;\n        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:in ( <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MilliM> ) ;\n        sh:description \"Unit must be millimetre for plate thickness (as declared in the schema).\" ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Note on material ambiguity:\n# The concrete mapping from (as‑built thickness, polar class,\n# material class) to a minimum steel grade is defined in Table 8 of\n# I2.12.1.  Because Table 8 is not reproduced in the supplied source\n# fragments, the SHACL graph records the need for this lookup but\n# does not encode a definitive enumerated grade list.  Consumers must\n# supply the table data or a custom SPARQL‑based validator to complete\n# the compliance check.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":65443,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":320,"cache_write_tokens":65120,"input_tokens_per_turn":[65443],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[320]},"output_tokens":2523,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1339,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[2523],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":67966},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}